# Hi-Fi RUSH (PPSA17168) -- title screen, first-boot language wizard, and on.
#
# Anchors are wall-clock seconds from the FIRST PAD POLL, not from process
# start, so the route is robust to how long the IoStore asset load takes -- on
# this title that varies by more than a minute between a cold and a warm page
# cache on the same machine.
#
# Windows are 3 s wide because a range shorter than the interval between pad
# polls can be missed entirely (tools/AGENTS.md).
#
# Run with PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG=1 so the route reports the transitions it
# actually delivered -- without it this route cannot tell "the guest ignored
# the input" from "the input was never applied".
#
# THE ROUTE IS A THREE-BEAT CYCLE, AND THE MIDDLE BEAT IS THE WHOLE POINT:
#
#     cross   -- confirm / Next
#     left    -- move a Yes/No dialog's selection off its default
#     cross   -- confirm again
#
# A cross-only route does NOT get past the language wizard, and it fails in the
# way that looks like a renderer wall rather than an input problem: pressing
# Next raises a "Continue with these settings?" dialog whose cursor starts on
# the RIGHT-HAND option, so every cross answers it in the negative and returns
# to the same page. Measured 2026-08-21 -- a 1168 s cross-only run cycled
# through that loop for its whole length with the guest healthy throughout.
# Same shape as the Tales of Graces f new-game dialogs (docs/TALES_GRACES_STATUS.md).

